## Why This Is Asked
Assess practical crypto hygiene, CMEK provisioning, tenant isolation, and operations around rotating keys without service downtime.

## Key Concepts

- CMEK per tenant with Azure Key Vault
- Encryption at rest for Cosmos DB with CMEK
- Per-tenant Managed Identities and RBAC
- Key rotation automation and rollback
- Policy and monitoring integration

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: create a CMEK and tie to Cosmos DB per tenant
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require("@azure/identity");
const { KeyClient } = require("@azure/keyvault-keys");
const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
const keyClient = new KeyClient(`https://<vault-name>.vault.azure.net`, credential);
await keyClient.createKey("cosmos-cmek-tenantA", "RSA" );
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test key rotation without impacting customers?
- How do you handle key compromise or vault access revocation?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to apply core Azure security controls (network, identities, policy) in a concrete, beginner-friendly scenario. It emphasizes least privilege, auditable changes, and rollback discipline.

## Key Concepts
- Private Endpoints and DENY public access for storage/sql
- User-Assigned Managed Identities for service-to-resource access
- Azure Policy to enforce private endpoints and deny public exposure
- Canary rollout and quick rollback plan with policy reversion

## Code Example
```json
// Policy (simplified) to deny public network access on storage and SQL
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "anyOf": [
        {"field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts"},
        {"field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Sql/servers"}
      ]
    },
    "then": {"effect": "deny"}
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify private endpoints are in effect across all resources?
- What tests ensure rollback can restore previous connectivity without downtime?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical use of CMK, Azure Policy, and Key Vault in a beginner-friendly scenario with rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Customer-managed keys (CMK) in Key Vault
- Azure Policy gating keySource and Key Vault linkage
- Managed identities for service access
- Rollback strategies and key rotation

## Code Example
```json
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "allOf": [
        {"equals": [{"field": "type"}, {"value": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts"}]},
        {"not": {"field": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/encryption.keySource", "equals": "Microsoft.KeyVault"}}
      ]
    },
    "then": {"effect": "deny"}
  }
}
```

